In article <2cteud$ocr@agate.berkeley.edu> kingunix@garnet.berkeley.edu (Rob Broekhuis) writes:
>Ah! So Fort Ludios is not the castle.  Had me fooled.  So yesterday I was
>leisurely strolling thru the dungeons and happened upon the portal to Ludios.
>Now, I've had many long games, I've even ascended, and never found Ludios
>before. What's it good for?

It's good for experience, to get you up to the quest requirements.  But the
main benefit is mucho gold, to give to your favorite priests.  Also, there
are usually many dragons there, making it a good source of intrinsics and
possible dragon scale mail.  It's also a good source of K-rations and
C-rations, which are quick to eat.  Finally, if you believe in polypiling,
all the soldiers make it an excellent source of armor to turn into GOP, SOR,
COD, HOT, and speed boots (and even an enchanted Hawaiian Shirt). (These, plus
GDSM, are my favorite armor. Your mileage may vary.)

This leads to two questions:

1) Is Fort Ludios always there?  Every time I've systematically looked for
   it, I've found it.

2) Is it possible to get dragon scales or dragon scale mail via polymorph?
   I never saw either, but I've decided polypiling makes the game too easy,
   so I only really tried it in one game (my first ascension).  Actually,
   that's not quite true.  One game the lighting shop only had one candle,
   so I polypiled tools for more.  In the future, I won't do that either,
   since I don't seem to use the castle's WOW (I once ascended carrying 
   effectively 11 unused wishes: two WOW and a magic lamp), so I'll just 
   use it for candles if I need them.

